    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0266",
      "sequence": 278,
      "meaning": "Seeing Sītā chosen, the cruel, ill-born and foolish kings become angry. The luckless men rise, put on armour and boast everywhere: seize Sītā, some say, and capture the two young princes. Merely breaking the bow does not complete the aim; while we live, who can marry the princess? If Videha gives any help, defeat him in battle along with the brothers. Hearing this, virtuous kings say their words shame the royal assembly: your strength, majesty, valour and greatness departed together with Pināka; where could such heroism be found now? With such judgment, fate has blackened your faces. Look upon Rāma to your eyes’ content and abandon envy, intoxication and anger; do not become moths after recognizing the fierce fire of Lakṣmaṇa’s wrath.",
