    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0269",
      "sequence": 281,
      "meaning": "Seeing Bhṛgupati’s fearsome guise, every terrified king rises. Each repeatedly names himself and his father while making full prostrations. Whoever Paraśurāma happens to regard kindly thinks his end has come. Janaka approaches again and bows his head, then summons Sītā and has her bow. He blesses her; her delighted, wise companions take her back to their party. Viśvāmitra then comes to meet him, and the two brothers place themselves at his lotus feet. On learning that Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa are Daśaratha’s sons, he blesses the handsome pair. His eyes tire from gazing fixedly at Rāma, whose boundless beauty breaks Love’s pride. Looking again toward Videha, Paraśurāma asks why such a great crowd has gathered; though he asks as if unaware, Janaka recognizes that anger has pervaded his whole body.",
