    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0270",
      "sequence": 282,
      "meaning": "Janaka reports the news and explains why all the kings assembled. Hearing him, Paraśurāma turns his gaze elsewhere and sees the pieces of the bow lying on the ground. In extreme fury he speaks harshly: tell me, witless Janaka, who broke this bow? Show him quickly, fool, or today I will overturn the earth as far as your kingdom extends. Terrified, the king gives no answer, while the crooked rulers rejoice inwardly. Gods, sages, Nāgas and the city’s men and women all worry with heavy fear. Sītā’s mother regrets that fate has ruined a matter it had just set right. Knowing Bhṛgupati’s nature, Sītā experiences half a blink like an age. Everyone looks fearfully upon timid Jānakī. Śrī Raghubīra, feeling neither joy nor sorrow, then speaks.",
